---
// The AI assistant page (issue #153/#604). Deliberately written in layman's
// terms — "talk to Claude or ChatGPT, it builds the bid, you review and send."
// The word "MCP" appears once, in the FAQ, for the technically curious and the
// search term. Every capability listed is verified against the live MCP tool
// surface (bids/line items/projects/phases/tasks/contacts/leads/site logs/
// change orders/summaries). This is an uncontested differentiator: no
// competitor offers a Claude/ChatGPT connection that operates their product.
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import FAQSection from '../../components/FAQSection.astro';
import CompareCta from '../../components/CompareCta.astro';
import { config } from '../../config';

const canDo = [
  'Start a bid from a plain-English description and build out its line items',
  'Price line items from your product catalog and labor rates',
  'Create contacts and leads from a name, a phone call, or an email thread',
  'Set up projects with phases and tasks, and update them as things change',
  'Log site notes and daily happenings from the field',
  'Draft change orders when the GC asks for something extra',
  'Answer questions: "What bids are still open?" "What\'s due this week?"',
  "Summarize a project, a customer history, or the month's billing",
];

const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'Do I need to be technical to use this?',
    answer:
      'No. If you can send a text message, you can use it. You connect BuildWorkPro to Claude or ChatGPT once, and from then on you just talk — describe the job, ask the question, request the change. There are no commands or prompts to memorize.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Which AI assistants work with BuildWorkPro?',
    answer:
      'Claude (on the web, desktop app, and phone) and ChatGPT — the two assistants most people already use. The connection uses an open standard, so as more assistants adopt it, they work too.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Can the assistant send a bid to my customer without me?',
    answer:
      'It works inside your account with your permissions, and the workflow that works is the one our founder uses: the assistant builds, you review in BuildWorkPro, and you decide what goes out. A bid reaches a customer when you send it.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Does the AI assistant cost extra?',
    answer:
      'No. Like everything else in BuildWorkPro, it is included in the $79/month plan — there is no AI add-on, token bill, or higher tier. You do need your own Claude or ChatGPT account.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What is this technically?',
    answer:
      'For the curious: the connection uses the Model Context Protocol (MCP), an open standard that lets AI assistants securely operate applications on your behalf. BuildWorkPro runs a live MCP server covering bids, projects, contacts, site logs, change orders, and more — the developer details are in our docs.',
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Build Construction Bids by Chatting with AI | BuildWorkPro"
  description="Connect BuildWorkPro to Claude or ChatGPT and build bids, projects, and site logs by talking — from your desk or your phone. You review and send. Included at $79/month."
>
  <Header />
  <main class="pt-32 pb-20">
    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 mb-16">
      <div class="text-center">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-brand-600 uppercase tracking-wider mb-3">
          AI assistant
        </p>
        <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 tracking-tight text-balance">
          Start your next bid by just describing it
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-slate-500 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
          BuildWorkPro connects to Claude and ChatGPT. Tell the assistant about the job — from your
          desk or your phone — and it builds the bid, the project, or the site log in your account.
          You review, then you send.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8">
          <CompareCta secondaryHref="#how-it-works" secondaryLabel="See how it works" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Founder proof -->
    <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 mb-20">
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-brand-100 bg-brand-50 p-8">
        <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
          "When I start a new bid, I usually just start chatting with Claude on my computer or my
          phone. I give it the information and it builds the bid for me. When it's done, I review it
          in BuildWorkPro and send it. Projects work the same way — the team and I run almost
          everything through natural conversation now."
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-slate-500">
          — Ivan, founder of BuildWorkPro and owner of
          <a
            href="/customers/national-glass/"
            class="text-brand-600 underline underline-offset-2 font-medium"
            >National Glass and Construction</a
          >
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- How it works -->
    <section id="how-it-works" class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 mb-20 scroll-mt-24">
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 text-center mb-10">How it works</h2>
      <ol class="space-y-6">
        {
          [
            [
              'Connect once',
              'Link BuildWorkPro to Claude or ChatGPT from your account — a few minutes, once, no technical setup beyond signing in. The step-by-step is in the docs.',
            ],
            [
              "Talk like you'd talk to your estimator",
              '"New bid for the Riverside storefront — twelve openings, our standard hardware, usual labor rates. Customer is Mendez Builders." The assistant creates the bid, adds the line items, and prices them from your catalog.',
            ],
            [
              'Review and send in BuildWorkPro',
              "Everything the assistant builds lands in your account looking like you made it — because it did it with your permissions. Open it, check the numbers, adjust what needs adjusting, and send it when it's right.",
            ],
          ].map(([title, body], i) => (
            <li class="flex gap-4">
              <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-brand-600 text-white flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold">
                {i + 1}
              </div>
              <div>
                <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-1">{title}</h3>
                <p class="text-slate-500 text-sm">{body}</p>
              </div>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </section>

    <!-- What it can do -->
    <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 mb-20">
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 text-center mb-10">
        What you can ask it to do
      </h2>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        {
          canDo.map((item) => (
            <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <svg
                class="w-5 h-5 text-brand-600 mt-0.5 shrink-0"
                fill="none"
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2.5"
                aria-hidden="true"
              >
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" />
              </svg>
              <span class="text-slate-600">{item}</span>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
      <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-slate-500 text-center max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        It works with your real account data — your
        <a
          href="/features/construction-bidding/"
          class="text-brand-600 underline underline-offset-2">catalog and labor rates</a
        >, your
        <a href="/features/construction-crm/" class="text-brand-600 underline underline-offset-2"
          >contacts and pipeline</a
        >, your
        <a href="/features/project-management/" class="text-brand-600 underline underline-offset-2"
          >projects</a
        > — under your permissions, with you as the final review.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Why nobody else has this -->
    <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 mb-20">
      <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
        <h2>The part nobody else offers</h2>
        <p>
          Plenty of construction software now advertises "AI" — a chatbot in a corner of their app,
          a summarizer, an autofill. This is different: BuildWorkPro connects to the assistant
          <em>you already talk to</em>, on the devices you already carry. You don't open the app to
          use the AI; you talk to Claude in your truck, and the bid is waiting in the app when you
          sit down. As of today, no other construction platform — not Procore, not Buildertrend, not
          JobTread, not Knowify — offers a Claude or ChatGPT connection that actually operates the
          product.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <FAQSection faqs={faqs} heading="AI assistant FAQ" />

    <!-- CTA -->
    <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center mt-20">
      <div class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-900 px-8 py-14 sm:px-14">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold text-white tracking-tight text-balance">
          Your estimator now takes voice notes
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-slate-400 max-w-xl mx-auto">
          Every feature, unlimited users, and the AI assistant connection — all in the one $79/month
          plan. Try the whole thing free for 14 days.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-center gap-4">
          <a
            href={config.signupUrl}
            class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-8 py-3.5 rounded-xl bg-brand-600 hover:bg-brand-700 text-white font-semibold text-sm transition-all hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:shadow-lg"
          >
            Start free trial
          </a>
          <a
            href="/api/mcp/overview/"
            class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-8 py-3.5 rounded-xl bg-white/10 text-white font-semibold text-sm hover:bg-white/20 transition-colors"
          >
            Setup guide in the docs
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-slate-500">
          <a href="/pricing/" class="text-slate-300 underline hover:text-white">$79/month flat</a> · 14-day
          free trial · No credit card required
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
